This is a bounded correction to the existing [65-obligation reuse register](https://github.com/Sodelin/Research-Commons/blob/e3f7097ca0704c59c7da541ad318572ea0ca2374/research/2026-10-10-codex-lean-rust-parity/reuse/OBLIGATION-REUSE-MAP.json), not a replacement ledger. The accepted baseline is [union1581](https://github.com/Sodelin/Research-Commons/tree/8839f3ba07a74888307c3cb6a8454eb13714c466/research/2026-10-11-dot-accepted-connected-union1581-0718z), whose complete audit is `c87ba37f9362b9dbc995bcb24903cb710e6b538455f406260da14cccb1ddc9b1`.

## Decisive finding

The checked library already contains the original scoped G1, timed G2 and binary M3 G5 endpoints, plus substantially more G6/G7 source and coefficient composition than some historical register statuses suggest. General G3 recognition and general G4 forcing remain mathematical obligations. G6's representative/cloud theorem and G7's finite-registry policy characterization are accepted hand mathematics with substantial formal assembly still missing. Module counts do not settle any of those quantifiers.

A literal pass through all65 existing IDs finds240 of267 declaration-reference occurrences in the1581 audit. This is a locator check, not a completion fraction. Direct source reading separates stale prototype names, real omitted modules and standalone executable entrypoints.

